<!--
  Plan 5 Task 4/6 phase 2: adaptive icon MONOCHROME layer (API 33+ "themed icons" / Material You -
  system Settings > Wallpaper & style > Themed icons), updated for the FINAL mark. Same 4
  shapes/coordinates as ic_launcher_foreground.xml (disc + ticks + needle + dot - see that file's
  own kdoc, and store-assets/brand/final/terrawatch-mark-monochrome.svg + final-rationale.md, for
  the full geometry/rationale), but every fillColor/strokeColor here is opaque white: per
  Android's own themed-icon guidance, the system reads ONLY this layer's alpha channel and
  re-tints the visible pixels with its own dynamic accent color, so the literal color is inert
  (same "alpha channel is all that matters" rule ic_stat_terrawatch.xml documents for the
  notification small icon) - white is used here purely by convention.

  The four ticks keep their 0.6 alpha (as strokeAlpha) rather than being forced fully opaque -
  after the OS's own re-tint this reads as a correspondingly fainter version of the tint color,
  preserving the same "ticks are quieter than the needle" relationship the full-color mark has.
  Disc/needle/dot are fully opaque, matching this file's own established "opaque wherever a
  shape is drawn" precedent from the previous shield design.
-->
